atic nominee James Martin, a first-time challenger who won a contested August primary. The independent candidate has raised almost nothing.\n\nEvery major rating outlet, including the Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, and Sabato's Crystal Ball, calls the race Solid or Safe Republican, with the most cautious at Likely Republican. Prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-ten chance. Coverage shows a conventional campaign: Martin emphasizing cost of living and clean water, Mast touting water-resources and other legislation. With no public polling available, the available evidence uniformly points to a comfortable Mast win, with the main open question being the final margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.066, "margin": -9.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.058, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0551, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0462, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0554, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0644, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0435, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0442, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.082, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -11.0}]}